r right now  prosecutors don't pay a lot of attention  to that new allegations claim  gates sent money to an accused sex  trafficker joel greenberg  who then gave it to three young women in  2018  greenberg is expected to plead guilty to  federal crimes as part of an undisclosed  deal  i'm sure matt gates is not feeling very  comfortable today the house committee is  looking into a variety of violations  including that gates allegedly shared  inappropriate images or videos while in  house chambers  if in fact these allegations are true of  course being removed from the judiciary  committee  is the least that could be done gates a  once rising star among conservatives  denies all the allegations against him  jennifer johnson global news  washington still ahead brazil's  climbing death toll from cover 19 and  still the president downplays the virus  you're watching global national  [Music]  for the first time in this pandemic  brazil's daily death toll surpassed  4 000 people the country's president has  long  downplayed the risks of the virus  encouraging regions to avoid lockdown  but this is where the p1 variant was  first detected the one that's more  contagious  and has the potential to lower the  effectiveness of some vaccines  here's mike drillet in sao paulo brazil  a ghoulish scene is playing out for the  world to see  workers exhuming bodies from old  graveyards to make room for more  with no end to the misery in sight  brazilians have now put their faith in  the covid19 vaccines  which the government was late in  ordering and are in short supply  it gives us hope that there are better  days ahead says this community leader  the numbers tell a different story more  than 345  000 brazilians have died from covet 19.  second only to the united states  however brazil surpassed 4 000 deaths in  one day this past week  and experts now predict it will surpass  the us in total deaths  by july even as health officials raise  alarms about the dangers of the more  transmissible p1 variant  which has also appeared in canada little  is being done to slow its spread  it's a pity we've become an  embarrassment to the world says this  union leader  brazil is a time bomb and breeding  ground for the coronavirus  much of the blame is being heaped on  president jair bolsonaro  an ally of former u.s president donald  trump  bolsonaro has refused to take the  vaccine openly derided lockdowns and  masks  and told brazilians to stop whining  about the virus  this virus like others is here to stay  and will remain for a lifetime he said  it is practically impossible to  eradicate what are we going to do until  then  medicine and supplies to treat covet 19  are running dangerously low  if the health care system collapses as  doctors in overwhelmed hospitals warn  is possible they may not be able to do  much  microlight global news toronto  up next the lessons teachers need to  help racialize students  in the past year remote learning has  blurred the line between classrooms and  living rooms  it's given parents new insight into what  their kids are learning  and what lessons are lacking in toronto  a group of black fathers is calling for  change  as candice daniel explains what started  as a conversation  among friends has transformed into a  campaign for equity  in education it all started here  in a local park the dads have been  friends for years and have grown into a  support network  for each other what's up fellas how you  guys doing  going public on youtube well this is a  first  we came together today just to have a  quick conversation about  some of our feelings about about growing  up black and having our kids grow up  black  in east york and being part of the  education system  in march they decided to take action  when the pandemic gave them  new insights into what was being said in  their kids remote classes  first i want to preface that i'm a  teacher the teachers have my full  support  that being said i don't think that  there's proper  training for teachers to talk about race  so they made this video about their  experiences  and what they hoped to see in education  and they sent the video to their  children's principals  and vice principals inclusive language  inclusive literature and representation  those are three things that we said to  these principals these are things that  you can do this is low hanging fruit  funke specializes in the history of  canada's education system  there are people in our school boards  there are people who are working  in the ministry of education who are  deeply invested  in creating models and creating  important  language that educators need to use and  adapt and  take into the classroom but for some  reason there is this disconnect  part of the problem she says is there  isn't a standard level of training for  canadian teachers  it differs from province to province  there are educators in individual  classrooms that are thinking critically  about how to address and speak to their  black students and then there are  schools that aren't doing it well  and as a result we don't have a uniform  way of understanding whether or not  we're doing it right  at the time of our interview only one of  four schools had acknowledged receiving  the video  and the father's offer to help global  news contacted the schools  and since then all principals have  reached out to the respective dads  i don't know what the next step is but i  hope this can start a conversation a  deeper conversation about what are we  really doing  are we ticking boxes or are we really  doing something different  and that i don't have the answer to  candace daniel  global news for more on candace's  conversation with the fathers and the  change they hope to see  be sure to watch the new reality tonight  at 7 pm  on global and that is global national  for this saturday night  i'm robin gill tonight your canada is  the port credit lighthouse  in mississauga we would love to see your  corner of the country so  please keep sending your photos thank  you for watching and i'll see you back  here tomorrow  have a great night
 

